<FILE_CONTENT name="README.md" target-output-path="../../packages/convo-lang-tools/README.md" dirty file-hash="6736465d0dc419fbd0f5cfd4ce5bdfc37159ce99" last-commit="9d789a6f341f99c5606617bb805af463c1bbca4a" closing-escape="((CLOSE_TAG[FILE_CONTENT]))" find-replace>
``` md
- Inline action on message groups: `Apply All`. This writes every file and runs every script in
  the message after a single confirmation. Find-replace blocks targeting the same file are
  combined into one write.
- Documents can be pinned so they stay in the view while you work in other files. Clicking a
  document item switches the view to that document.
//// replace-with ////
- Inline action on message groups: `Review`. This starts a guided review of the file blocks in the
  message. See [Guided review](#guided-review).
- Inline action on message groups: `Apply All`. This writes every file and runs every script in
  the message after a single confirmation. Find-replace blocks targeting the same file are
  combined into one write.
- Documents can be pinned so they stay in the view while you work in other files. Clicking a
  document item switches the view to that document.

### Guided review

The `Review` action on a message group in the Code Blocks view walks through every `FILE_CONTENT`
block in the message, one block at a time.

- Files are reviewed in the order they first appear in the message.
- A single diff tab is reused. It is replaced when the review moves to the next file.
- The diff is cumulative. For find-replace blocks, the proposed side shows the current file with
  every block up to the current one applied.
- Each block's changes are marked with a divider and a label, such as
  `── block #3 · find-replace · ✓ accepted ──`. Block numbers start at 1 and follow the order of
  blocks in the message. Full file blocks are labeled on the first line.
- The current block has a solid divider, a `▶` prefix and highlighted lines.
- `Next` moves to the next change in the current block, then to the next block. `Previous` moves
  back. `Skip File` jumps to the first block of the next file.
- Blocks are accepted by default. Click the status bar item, or press `Ctrl+Alt+\`, to accept or
  reject the current block. The status bar shows progress, such as `Block 2/5 ✓ · Change 1/3`.
- After the last block, a dialog offers `Apply Accepted Files` and `Restart Review`. If the message
  contains scripts, it also offers `Apply Files and Run Scripts`.
- Rejected blocks are skipped when the accepted blocks of a file are combined and written.

| Action         | Keybinding     | Notification button |
|----------------|----------------|---------------------|
| Next change    | `Ctrl+Alt+]`   | `Next`              |
| Previous change| `Ctrl+Alt+[`   | `Previous`          |
| Skip file      |                | `Skip File`         |
| Toggle accept  | `Ctrl+Alt+\`   |                     |
| Cancel         |                | `Cancel`            |
```
</FILE_CONTENT>

<FILE_CONTENT name="README.md" target-output-path="../../packages/convo-lang-tools/README.md" dirty file-hash="6736465d0dc419fbd0f5cfd4ce5bdfc37159ce99" last-commit="9d789a6f341f99c5606617bb805af463c1bbca4a" closing-escape="((CLOSE_TAG[FILE_CONTENT]))" find-replace>
``` md
| Convo: Apply All Code Blocks In Message| `convo.code-block-group-apply-all`         | Writes all files and runs all scripts in a message             |
//// replace-with ////
| Convo: Apply All Code Blocks In Message| `convo.code-block-group-apply-all`         | Writes all files and runs all scripts in a message             |
| Convo: Review Code Blocks In Message   | `convo.code-block-group-review`            | Starts a guided review of the file blocks in a message         |
| Convo: Review Next Change              | `convo.code-block-review-next`             | Moves to the next change or block (`Ctrl+Alt+]`)               |
| Convo: Review Previous Change          | `convo.code-block-review-previous`         | Moves to the previous change or block (`Ctrl+Alt+[`)           |
| Convo: Review Skip File                | `convo.code-block-review-skip-file`        | Jumps to the first block of the next file                      |
| Convo: Review Toggle Accept            | `convo.code-block-review-toggle-accept`    | Accepts or rejects the current block (`Ctrl+Alt+\`)            |
| Convo: Review Cancel                   | `convo.code-block-review-cancel`           | Ends the review and closes the diff                            |
```
</FILE_CONTENT>

Notes:
- **`replaceCount` change:** it now counts only the replacements actually made. Before, it counted every match, including matches beyond the `find-replace` limit. Existing callers only check whether it is zero, so they behave the same.
- **One notification at a time:** VSCode can't dismiss notifications from code. When you navigate with keybindings, the open notification stays as is. The status bar always shows the current progress.
- **Keybindings:** the review keybindings only apply while a review is active (`convo.codeBlockReviewActive`). They use `Ctrl+Alt` on every platform because `Cmd+Alt+[` and `Cmd+Alt+]` are fold and unfold on macOS.
- **Review command placement:** `Convo: Review Code Blocks In Message` is hidden from the Command Palette because it needs a message group. The navigation commands only appear in the palette during a review.


