``` md
| Convo: Review Next Change              | `convo.code-block-review-next`             | Moves to the next change or block (`Ctrl+Alt+]`)               |
| Convo: Review Previous Change          | `convo.code-block-review-previous`         | Moves to the previous change or block (`Ctrl+Alt+[`)           |
| Convo: Review Skip File                | `convo.code-block-review-skip-file`        | Jumps to the first block of the next file                      |
| Convo: Review Toggle Accept            | `convo.code-block-review-toggle-accept`    | Accepts or rejects the current block (`Ctrl+Alt+\`)            |
//// replace-with ////
| Convo: Review Next Change              | `convo.code-block-review-next`             | Moves to the next change or file (`Ctrl+Alt+]`)                |
| Convo: Review Previous Change          | `convo.code-block-review-previous`         | Moves to the previous change or file (`Ctrl+Alt+[`)            |
| Convo: Review Skip File                | `convo.code-block-review-skip-file`        | Jumps to the first change of the next file                     |
| Convo: Review Toggle Accept            | `convo.code-block-review-toggle-accept`    | Accepts or rejects the current block (`Ctrl+Alt+\`)            |
| Convo: Review Finish                   | `convo.code-block-review-finish`           | Opens the apply dialog once no block is pending                |
```
</FILE_CONTENT>

Notes:
- **Status bar toggle:** a pending block becomes accepted on the first toggle. After that, it switches between accepted and rejected.
- **Internal commands:** `convo.code-block-review-set-status` and `convo.code-block-review-goto` are only called from code lenses. They aren't declared in `package.json`, so they don't appear in the Command Palette.
- **Label lens:** the label lens uses an empty command, so clicking it does nothing.
- **`diffEditor.codeLens` scope:** the setting is changed in user settings only. If a workspace setting turns it off, the workspace value wins and the lenses won't show.


